  "fails_if": "`resolve_representation_cases` (source_representations.py) stops passing an applied entry's field permission to formation, so units and texts keep conflicting names and form no variable; or formation copies one edition's unit or text onto the other state; or it lets a name permission settle overlap's same-column unit conflict (no conflicting_occurrence_facts, a written unit); or it stops comparing an entry's expected codings with the built coding, so coded applies without stale_representation_coding; or a checked [[errata.field]] name correction is waived by the name permission (fixname forms a variable)",
  "note": "One SCB register per claim; register N delivers column VALUE as variable N (CVIDs N01 and N02, editions N20 and N21). Each `[[representation.delivery_metadata]]` entry permits the listed source texts over both of its records and the column window 2020-01-01..2021-12-31 (overlap: 2020 only). units: 2020 'Income 2020' in '100-tal kronor', 2021 'Income 2021' in 'Kronor (SEK)', names permitted. bare: the same rows without an entry, the baseline. overlap: both rows in 2020 with the two units. texts: 2020 'Visit'/'Visited facility', 2021 'Admission'/'Admitting facility', one unit, names and descriptions permitted. descriptions: the same rows, only descriptions permitted. coded: the units rows, authored without a code list and built with one Vardemangder list on CVID 601 (2020 only). fixname and fixunit: the units rows plus an `[[errata.field]]` on CVID N01 setting the name or the unit to 'Checked source wording'. Expected values are the replaced tests' assertions restated per register; rows the replaced tests did not assert are derived from the fixture: a variable whose two editions keep different names forms no variable (unresolved_variable_name), two different units in one variable warn delivery_units_vary, and coded's list covers only 2020 (missing_coding_period for 2021).",
